# probes_negative/ fixture — deliberately broken, NOT donor-faithful.
# Derived from the same ScoreRow shape as the sibling
# annotated/tests/integration/test_writes/pandas_score_dataset.pyk.
# The annotated sibling uses the canonical `PandasFrame[X]` v1.3
# form; this fixture uses the deprecated `DataFrame[X]` alias to
# assert that pykrete fires D0090 (deprecatedDataFrameAlias) per
# docs/design/pandas-support.md §6.
#
# Failure mode exercised: D0090 fires once per `DataFrame[X]`
# parameter annotation slot (v1.3 deprecation warning).
#
# Naming note: this file lives next to the pandas additions because
# v1.3 introduces D0090 alongside the PandasFrame[X] surface, but the
# diagnostic itself is dialect-agnostic — DataFrame[X] is now the
# generic alias regardless of pandas vs Spark routing, and the same
# .pyk would fire under a Spark-typed receiver too.

